course: dictionary
lesson: 9183
title: Words for crying
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sobbing is crying loudly with short, noisy breaths, usually because you are very sad or upset. You can use it as a noun («the sobbing») or as a verb: «She sobbed all night» means she cried in this way for a long time.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The Gryphon thumps the sobbing Mock Turtle: «Same as if he had a bone in his throat.»» The Turtle is crying in short, noisy breaths, and the Gryphon thumps his back, so sobbing must mean crying like this.
explain: Sobbing is stronger than a small cry. Adults often hug a sobbing child, because the child is very upset. Phrases like «burst into sobbing» and «sobbing uncontrollably» tell you the crying started suddenly or could not be stopped.
fact: Sobbing means crying loudly with short, noisy breaths.
fact: The verb forms are sob, sobs, sobbed and sobbing.
fact: «Sobbing» can also be a noun, as in «the sobbing».
fact: «Sob your heart out» means to cry very hard for a long time.
fact: «A sob story» is a sad story told to make people feel sorry for someone.
exercise: «The sobbing child hugged her teddy bear.» What does sobbing mean here? | Sleeping very quietly | *Crying loudly with short, noisy breaths | Running fast across the playground | Singing a happy song
exercise: The Gryphon thumps the sobbing Mock Turtle: «Same as if he had a bone in his throat.» Which word in this sentence shows the Mock Turtle is crying? | throat | thumps | *sobbing | same
exercise: Which phrase means crying very hard and for a long time? | *sobbing uncontrollably | sobbing in a quiet library | a sob story | sobbing is a good dance move
test: Sobbing is the same as laughing. True or false? | *False | True
test: Which word is a verb form of sobbing in «She sobbed all night»? | *sobbed | night | She | all
exam: In «The Gryphon thumps the sobbing Mock Turtle», what is the Mock Turtle doing? | Reading a book | *Crying with short, noisy breaths | Sleeping under a tree | Dancing
